 git log --oneline | head -2; git diff 89bcef9 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-900", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /tmp && rm -rf ow && git clone -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" ow; cd ow && git log --oneline | head -2; git diff 89bcef9 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-900"]], "output": "```console\n4feb80b Outline: C2 wording rule, C4 (ii) near-null (idea-review v3)\n89bcef9 Outline v3: accepted analysis amendments (truth = pool minus S, primary cells, C2 tolerance, contingency)\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-- **C2 tolerance (amended, replaces 0.01/25%):** \"tracks\" = calibration slope CI contains 1 and MAE ≤ max(0.005, 1.5 × median between-pool SE of the cell gaps, 25% of the mean measured gap). Primary predictor = the refined one (parametric bootstrap from shrunken θ̂); κσ̄/√n is judged as an upper end (\"holds\" = measured gap ≤ predicted in ≥ 90% of cells, with the between-pool interval).\n-- **C4 nulls:** (i) synthetic equal-θ worlds fitted to the real item-level structure; (ii) real configurations in the densest 0.02-wide window of full-pool accuracy (window chosen by count; dropped, and said so, if < 20 configurations). Rates per scenario × n ∈ {60, 120, 240} × budget ratio {1, 4}.\n+- **C2 tolerance (amended, replaces 0.01/25%):** \"tracks\" = calibration slope CI contains 1 and MAE ≤ max(0.005, 1.5 × median between-pool SE of the cell gaps, 25% of the mean measured gap). Primary predictor = the refined one (parametric bootstrap from shrunken θ̂); κσ̄/√n is judged as an upper end (\"holds\" = measured gap ≤ predicted in ≥ 90% of cells, with the between-pool interval). **Wording rule (added after idea-review of v3):** the delivered result states which term set the tolerance (0.005, the SE term, or 25%). \"Tracks\" is written only when the 25% or 0.005 term sets it and the slope CI excludes 0; when the SE term sets the tolerance, or the slope CI contains both 0 and 1, the outcome is worded \"consistent with the predictor, not discriminating\".\n+- **C4 nulls:** (i) synthetic equal-θ worlds fitted to the real item-level structure; (ii) real configurations in the densest 0.02-wide window of full-pool accuracy (window chosen by count; dropped, and said so, if < 20 configurations). **(ii) is a near-null, not a null** (true θ can differ by up to 0.02, within test power at n = 240): the \"above nominal\" (nominal + 1 pp) judgement is made on (i) only; (ii) is reported as near-null with the pool-accuracy spread in the window beside each rate, and no \"above nominal\" is read from it. Rates per scenario × n ∈ {60, 120, 240} × budget ratio {1, 4}.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "9f43f863-6da9-5af6-beb9-4fbd122cbae7", "at": 1795649929.6032727, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19987, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "467f72ca173c549dcbd298d5e273a575", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "f9806ea6-6df3-55d2-91c4-a5c9325bc18d", "at": 1795649929.6133807, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19988, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "467f72ca173c549dcbd298d5e273a575", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "3f29315b-1f59-5f3e-9e0e-8ef45571673b", "at": 1795649929.6598687, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 19992, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "467f72ca173c549dcbd298d5e273a575", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "